Negative control for the picker offering ONE ENTRY PER CONTROL the table
declares (`R6-35`), not per column it happens to be drawing.

Builds the options from the DRAWN columns rather than the declared ones. It
reads as a one-word simplification and is a one-way door: a column the user
takes off leaves the menu with it, so nothing can ever put it back and the only
recovery is editing the url by hand. Hiding still works, the url still carries
the set, the default set is still the declaration's — only the option list is on
trial.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the column-set spec — after a column is hidden the picker no longer offers
it, so the "every declared column stays offerable" case fails and the case that
switches a hidden column back on fails with it.

